ga14(){return"Le Quang Liem beats Grischuk"},
ga13(){return"FIDE World Cup, Troms\xf8 2013. Le Quang Liem (2702) with White against Alexander Grischuk (2785), then a world top-ten player. There is no sacrifice here: just a squeeze, a trade of every heavy piece, and a won pawn ending. This is how real games are usually decided."},
ga87(){return"Gr\xfcnfeld Exchange: Black lets White build a big pawn centre, planning to shoot at it with pieces. Double-edged from move five."},
ga88(){return"Bh6 trades Black's g7 bishop \u2014 the strongest piece in the Gr\xfcnfeld, the one holding the long diagonal. Trading it removes the backbone of Black's position."},
ga89(){return"d5 gains space and shuts the b7 bishop out of the game. From here Black's pieces have fewer and fewer squares."},
